From 5a292c2273cce1f057d4cb89552a9fbb6857f203 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kernel-rg35xx <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:55:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] atc260x_power: RG35XX board support recovered from the
 vendor kernel

Recovered from the RG35XX running kernel (3.10.37 ctalon #40, binary only)
by function-level comparison; the charger struct layout matches the device.

- Rumble motor on the PWM of the absent external DC-DC (DT pwms "ext_moto",
  ext_dcdc_exist = 0): sysfs "moto", 0..100 % duty, started stopped.
- Status LEDs: work and low-battery LED pairs, a second charge-LED pin
  ("_new" DT properties: the board revisions use one pin or the other),
  driven by a 500 ms poll on system_wq (allen_led_poll) that the first
  charging-monitor run starts; it replaces led_state_charge/normal. sysfs
  "led_test" blinks every LED (factory test).
- USB OTG: ID input, switch and VBUS-enable outputs; the poll powers the
  port while the ID pin reads high.
- ldo5 rail enabled at probe.
- no_screen (DT): there is no owl backlight to ask, so the charge current
  uses the screen-on limits (screen-off ones in charger boot mode).
- Battery temperature control (DT temp_ctl_enable, off in the RG35XX DTS):
  protective power-off via owl_force_shutdown(), charging stopped outside a
  window and resumed with hysteresis.
- Charger status changes are logged.

Deliberate differences from the vendor binary: the repeated GPIO blocks use
two helpers, absent or busy pins are skipped instead of driven, and
shutdown also stops the LED poll before freeing its GPIOs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
